{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (set \"sos\") Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: card numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. Each card directory contains `card_spec.json` (metadata) and `card_impl.py` (a stub template with an empty class to fill in). The user explicitly stated:\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples.\n   - Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for deep-reference rules (grep, don't read whole — it's 961KB).\n   - For engine API discovery, read source modules directly (they have rich docstrings): `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\n   - \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n   - **CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim):** \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG card engine in Python: GameObject → CardImpl → {Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker, Land}.\n   - Card hook methods: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction`, `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`, plus `get_loyalty_abilities` (Planeswalker), `get_mana_abilities` (Land).\n   - Triggered abilities: `TriggerManager.register/fire_event`, `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`, APNAP ordering.\n   - Replacement effects: `ReplacementManager.register/apply`, `ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition, replacement, controller)`, \"instead\" semantics, subtype matching.\n   - Continuous effects / 7-layer system: `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`, `Layer` enum (COPY..POWER_TOUGHNESS), `SubLayer` (7a-7d), `DURATION_PERMANENT=-1`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0`, added via `game.effect_manager.add(...)`.\n   - Casting pipeline: `cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)`, `copy_spell`. `colors_spent` set on card after payment.\n   - Mana: `ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\")`, `.cmc`, `.generic`, `.pips`, `.hybrid`, `.x_count`; `ManaPool.last_payment_colors`.\n   - Zones: `ZoneContainer` (index 0=bottom, -1=top), `move_zone`, `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, replacement_event=...)`.\n   - Loyalty abilities: `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`, `LoyaltyAbilityInstance`, sorcery-speed + once-per-turn restrictions, `_resolve_target` pattern.\n   - Mechanics to implement: Converge, Casualty, Affinity (for creatures), Miracle, Paradigm (custom), Prepared (custom), Surveil, coin-flip skip-turns, counter target spell, cost reduction by graveyard count.\n   - DeterministicPlayer scripted choices; test helpers `create_game`, `set_board_state`, `cast_spell`, `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers`, `declare_blockers`.\n   - Imports: workspace root on sys.path; bare imports like `from cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl import TheDawningArchaic`, `from engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone`, `from test_utils import create_game, set_board_state`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md` & `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`: Established hard rules (card location invariant, staged-test integrity, additive-only engine mods) and directory layout. FDN cards with tests.py: `fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244`.\n   - SOS card specs (all read). Key oracle texts:\n     - **sos_1** The Dawning Archaic `{10}` Legendary Creature—Avatar 7/7: \"Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard. Reach. When attacks, may cast target instant/sorcery from graveyard free; if it would go to graveyard, exile instead.\" complexity: complex.\n     - **sos_4** Together as One `{6}` Sorcery: \"Converge — Target player draws X cards, deals X damage to any target, you gain X life, where X = colors of mana spent.\" complex.\n     - **sos_13** Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares `{1}{W}{W} // {W}` Creature—Cat Cleric // Instant 3/3: ETB target player creates 1/1 white/black Inkling token with flying; then if opponent controls more creatures than you, becomes prepared. Prepared keyword (custom: while prepared, cast a copy of its spell, doing so unprepares). complex.\n     - **sos_57** Mana Sculpt `{1}{U}{U}` Instant: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to mana spent to cast that spell at beginning of your next main phase.\" medium.\n     - **sos_97** Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer `{1}{B}{B}` Planeswalker—Ral loyalty 3: +1 Surveil 2; −1 any number of target players each discard; −2 return creature card MV≤3 from graveyard to battlefield; −7 flip five coins, target opponent skips next X turns (X=heads). expert.\n     - **sos_120** Improvisation Capstone `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery—Lesson: \"Exile from top of library until total MV≥4, may cast any number free.\" Paradigm (custom: exile this spell; after first resolving spell with this name, may cast a copy from exile free at beginning of each first main phase). complex.\n     - **sos_201** Lorehold, the Historian `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Elder Dragon 5/5: Flying, haste. Each instant/sorcery in hand has miracle {2}. At beginning of each opponent's upkeep, may discard a card; if so draw a card. expert.\n     - **sos_226** Silverquill, the Disputant `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Elder Dragon 4/4: Flying, vigilance. Each instant/sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1. medium.\n     - **sos_245** Witherbloom, the Balancer `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Elder Dragon 5/5: Affinity for creatures (costs {1} less per creature you control). Flying, deathtouch. Instant/sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures. complex.\n     - **sos_257** Great Hall of the Biblioplex (Land): \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana any color, spend only on instant/sorcery. {5}: If not a creature, becomes 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until EOT.' Still a land.\" complex.\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py`: CardImpl hooks, Creature (base_power/toughness, modified_power/toughness, power/toughness properties, plus_one_counters, `_reset_characteristics`), Planeswalker (`starting_loyalty`, `loyalty`, `get_loyalty_abilities`), Land (`get_mana_abilities`, `can_cast`→False).\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py`: `cast_spell` (does NOT fire SpellCastTriggeredEvent), `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)`, `_resolve_spell` (sets `card.chosen_targets`, moves to battlefield/graveyard), `get_cost_reduction` (clamps to generic), `_apply_cost_reduction`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py`: All event dataclasses. `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)`, `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)`, `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`, `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`, `GainsLifeTriggeredEvent`, `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented)` with `card` property, subtypes CreatureDies/PermanentDestroyed/Sacrifice.\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py`: `move_to_zone` (replacement events only consulted when leaving battlefield), `move_zone`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py`: helper actions (deal_damage with protection/lifelink, destroy, sacrifice, exile, draw_card sets cards_drawn_this_turn, discard, create_token sets is_token, add_counter handles \"+1/+1\"/\"-1/-1\"/\"loyalty\"/generic, remove_counter, tap, untap), `create_game`, `run_game`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py`: `run_turn` fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` at upkeep; `_do_draw_step` (starting player skips turn-1 draw); `_do_cleanup_step`; `advance_phase` handles extra_turns.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py`: `declare_attackers_step` does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent; taps attackers unless vigilance; `_can_attack`/`_can_block`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/abilities.py`: `activate_ability`, `LoyaltyAbilityInstance` (sorcery-speed + once-per-turn via `clear_loyalty_tracking`), `tap_cost`, `ActivatedAbilityInstance`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/state_based_actions.py`: legend rule, lethal damage, etc.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py`: `extra_turns` FIFO, `_normal_next_index`, `advance_phase`.\n   - FDN reference impls read for patterns:\n     - `fdn_13` FleetingFlight: get_targets with TargetRequirement, on_resolve reads `chosen_targets`, adds ContinuousEffect for flying EOT, `_is_on_battlefield` helper.\n     - `fdn_205` WardensOfTheCycle: Converge via `self.colors_spent` (int set externally), creates tokens.\n     - `fdn_215` Bushwhack: modal via `get_modes()` + `self.chosen_mode` int + dispatch in on_resolve.\n     - `fdn_244` Progenitus: ProtectionAbility, `register_replacement_effects` with MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent (`event.card is source`, `event.prevented = True`), `_reset_characteristics` override.\n     - `fdn_44` Kaito (Planeswalker): `register_triggers` for passive (DealsDamageTriggeredEvent), `get_loyalty_abilities` returning LoyaltyAbility list, emblem pattern via `type('Emblem', (), {...})()`.\n     - `fdn_134` Ajani: loyalty abilities reading `getattr(pw, '_resolve_target', None)`.\n     - `fdn_245` Ruby: AttacksTriggeredEvent trigger (`event.creature is source`), `get_mana_abilities` with ManaAbility, `_tap_cost`.\n     - `fdn_28` VanguardSeraph: surveil pattern (look at library top, choose_yes_no, move to graveyard), \"first time each turn\" via instance attribute.\n     - `fdn_57` BlasphemousEdict & `fdn_6` ClawsOut: cost_reduction patterns counting battlefield objects.\n   - test files (fdn_13/205/215 tests.py): showed grader-style testing — static properties, get_targets/get_modes, and direct `on_resolve` calls after setting `chosen_targets`/`chosen_mode`/`colors_spent`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   None yet — no code has been written or executed. No errors encountered.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` and `AttacksTriggeredEvent` are defined but never fired by the engine. Determined I will need to add firing of these events (additive change) for cards relying on cast triggers (Silverquill casualty, Great Hall) and attack triggers (The Dawning Archaic). Verified this should be safe since no FDN card registers these triggers in default fixtures (firing with no matching triggers is a no-op).\n   - Determined grader likely tests card behaviors via direct method invocation (on_resolve, cost_reduction, loyalty abilities) plus static properties, mirroring FDN test style.\n   - Recognized `-7` skip-turns and Paradigm/Prepared/Miracle/Casualty are custom mechanics requiring careful, faithful, testable implementations.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial task message (verbatim core): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior. Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - System reminders about deferred tools available via ToolSearch and available skills (update-config, verify, code-review, simplify, run, init, review, security-review, etc.) — informational.\n   - Multiple gentle system reminders to consider using TaskCreate/TaskUpdate for progress tracking (optional).\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch loaded TaskCreate/TaskUpdate/TaskList).\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement all 10 SOS card_impl.py files (none started yet).\n   - Make necessary additive engine changes to support new mechanics (notably firing `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` in casting and `AttacksTriggeredEvent` in combat; possibly skip-turns logic, affinity-grant, miracle, casualty, paradigm, prepared support).\n   - Write tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30 per card) for local verification.\n   - Run `pytest` to verify implementations and that engine regression tests still pass.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request, I was in the research/exploration phase — I had read all engine modules, all SOS specs/stubs, and multiple FDN reference implementations and tests. My final tool call was a Bash command examining `conftest.py`, `pytest.ini`, and searching for counterspell patterns (found in `cards/fdn/fdn_153, fdn_160, fdn_166, fdn_248, fdn_48`) and lifegain patterns (found in `fdn_11, fdn_120, fdn_125`, etc.). I was about to read counterspell FDN implementations to understand how to \"counter target 