{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (set \"sos\") Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: card numbers **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**. Each card directory contains `card_spec.json` (metadata) and `card_impl.py` (a stub template with an empty class to fill in). The user's explicit instructions (verbatim core from original task):\n   - \"Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples.\"\n   - \"Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text\" (grep, don't read whole — 961KB).\n   - \"For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\"\n   - \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n   - **CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim):** \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - From AGENTS.md hard rules: card implementation class must stay in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py` (no move/rename); treat `engine_tests/` as read-only; do NOT edit existing FDN test files at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`; **additive-only engine modifications** — may add methods/classes/files in `engine/` and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete anything existing in `engine/`. Own SOS tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`, max 30 tests per card.\n   - Final user message: CRITICAL instruction to respond with TEXT ONLY (no tool calls) and produce this summary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG card engine in Python. Class hierarchy: `GameObject` → `CardImpl` → {Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker, Land}.\n   - CardImpl hooks: `can_cast(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)->int` (generic-only, clamped ≥0), `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)` (reads `self.chosen_targets`), `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers(game)`, `register_replacement_effects(game)`, `get_activated_abilities()`, `get_modes()`. Planeswalker adds `get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]`; Land adds `get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility]`.\n   - Creature: `base_power/base_toughness` (printed), `modified_power/modified_toughness` (set by layer 7c effects, reset to base each cycle), `power`/`toughness` properties = modified + plus_one_counters − minus_one_counters; `plus_one_counters`, `minus_one_counters`, `damage_marked`, `is_tapped`, `summoning_sick`, `is_attacking`, `is_token`. `_reset_characteristics()` resets these.\n   - Triggers: `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`; `game.trigger_manager.register/unregister(source)/fire_event(game, event)`. APNAP ordering. fire_event matches by isinstance (subclasses included); returns early (no-op) if no matching triggers.\n   - Replacement effects: `ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition, replacement, controller)`; `game.replacement_manager.register/apply`. Only consulted when leaving battlefield (in move_to_zone). `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent` has `.card` property, `.destination`, `.prevented`; subtypes CreatureDies/PermanentDestroyed/Sacrifice.\n   - Continuous effects (7 layers): `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`; `Layer` IntEnum (COPY=1..POWER_TOUGHNESS=7), `SubLayer` (7a..7d), `DURATION_PERMANENT=-1`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0`; `game.effect_manager.add(effect)`. apply_all resets objects then applies sorted effects.\n   - Casting pipeline (engine/casting.py): `cast_spell(game, player, card)` — timing/can_cast/hand/move-to-stack/choose targets/pay mana/on_cast/push StackObject; sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` — no mana/timing. `get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`, `_apply_cost_reduction(cost, reduction)`. `is_sorcery_speed`, `can_cast_at_instant_speed`. `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets`, then permanents→battlefield, instant/sorcery→graveyard via move_to_zone.\n   - Counterspell pattern (from fdn_48/fdn_153): helper `_counter_spell(game, stack_obj)` pops from `game.stack._items` by identity, removes card from controller's STACK zone, adds to owner's GRAVEYARD. `can_cast` returns True only if a (matching) spell is on stack. `get_targets` returns TargetRequirement with `zone=Zone.STACK`, filter checking `getattr(stack_obj, \"is_spell\", True)` or `CardType.CREATURE in source.card_types`. `_get_chosen_target(card, game)` reads `chosen_targets[0]` or falls back to `_resolve_target`.\n   - StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability). `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)` shallow-copies source card, binds on_resolve to copied card directly (no zone move).\n   - Mana: `ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\")`, `.cmc`, `.generic`, `.pips` (dict[ManaType,int]), `.x_count`, `.hybrid`. `ManaPool.add(ManaType, n)`, `.can_pay`, `.pay`, `.last_payment_colors` (list[Color], distinct, excludes colorless). `ManaType` enum has COLORLESS. `Color` enum (WHITE..GREEN).\n   - Zones: `ZoneContainer` (index 0=bottom, -1=top); `.add(obj, position=\"top\"/\"bottom\")`, `.remove`, `.contains`, `.get_all`, `.top(n)`, `.shuffle`. `move_zone(obj, from_container, to_container, position)`. `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)` — fires LBF/dies/ETB events, registers/unregisters triggers; replacement only consulted when leaving battlefield. `move_zone` deletes `colors_spent` on zone change.\n   - game.py helpers: `deal_damage(game, source, target, amount)` (player→life with DealsDamage+LosesLife events; creature→damage_marked; lifelink), `destroy`, `sacrifice`, `exile`, `draw_card(game, player)` (sets cards_drawn_this_turn, fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent), `discard`, `create_token(game, player, token)` (sets is_token, fires ETB, registers triggers), `add_counter(game, perm, counter_type, amount)` (handles \"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\", generic dict), `remove_counter`, `tap`, `untap`. No `gain_life` helper exists — add life directly and fire `GainsLifeTriggeredEvent(player, amount)`.\n   - Loyalty abilities: `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; `LoyaltyAbilityInstance`; sorcery-speed + once-per-turn (via `_loyalty_activated_this_turn`, `clear_loyalty_tracking()`). Loyalty ability effects read `getattr(pw, '_resolve_target', None)` for targets (see fdn_44/134).\n   - Planeswalker pattern (fdn_44 Kaito): `register_triggers` for passive (DealsDamageTriggeredEvent), `get_loyalty_abilities` returns list; emblem via `type('Emblem', (), {'name': ...})()` as trigger source; uses SpellCastTriggeredEvent.\n   - Surveil pattern (fdn_28): look at library top via `library.get_all()[-1]`, `choose_yes_no`, move to graveyard; \"first time each turn\" via instance attr `_..._on_turn` vs `game.turn_number`.\n   - Converge pattern (fdn_205 Wardens): `self.colors_spent` (int 0 in __init__, used as count via range()); but the REAL pipeline sets colors_spent to a LIST — so robust code must handle both int and list.\n   - extra_turns: `game.extra_turns` (FIFO list of player seat indices) handled in advance_phase; `_normal_next_index`. No skip-turn mechanism exists in engine.\n   - turn.py run_turn: fires BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent at upkeep; _do_draw_step (starting player skips turn-1 draw); main phases (step=None) previously just granted priority (now fire BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent — my addition). _do_cleanup_step removes EOT effects, clears damage/combat flags, empties mana pools. Mana pools empty on EVERY phase/step transition (advance_phase + empty_mana_pools).\n   - combat.py: declare_attackers_step taps attackers unless VIGILANCE; _can_attack/_can_block; previously did NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent (now fires — my addition). Flying blocked only by flying/reach. Deathtouch/trample/lifelink handled.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: scripted `choose_target`, `choose`, `choose_yes_no`, `assign_damage_order`, `choose_card` all pop from `_script` deque. test_utils helpers prepend to `_script`.\n   - test_utils.py: `create_game(deck1, deck2, *, player1_name, player2_name, player1_life, player2_life, scripts)`; `set_board_state(game, idx, *, battlefield, hand, graveyard, life, mana)` (mana is dict[ManaType,int]); `cast_spell(game, idx, card_name, targets=None)` (finds by name, sets sorcery timing, scripts targets, casts, resolves whole stack); `advance_to_phase`; `declare_attackers(game, names)`; `declare_blockers(game, {attacker: [blockers]})`; `card_colors(card)`.\n   - Grader test style (from fdn_13 tests.py): tests static properties (isinstance, name, mana_cost), get_targets returns list of TargetRequirement with correct zone and filter_fn behavior, on_resolve called directly after setting `spell.chosen_targets = [...]` (no-target = no-op must not raise).\n   - Imports: workspace root on sys.path; bare imports `from cards.sos.sos_4.card_impl import TogetherAsOne`, `from engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Supertype, TargetRequirement, Zone`, `from test_utils import create_game, set_board_state`.\n   - Environment: use `python3` (not `python`). `pytest.ini` has `python_files = test_*.py tests.py`; \"timeout\" config option warning is benign (pytest-timeout not installed).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` (MODIFIED, 3 edits):\n     - get_cost_reduction now consults static cost reducers on controller's battlefield (for \"affinity granted to your spells\" mechanic — Witherbloom sos_245):\n       ```python\n       battlefield = controller.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD]\n       for perm in battlefield.get_all():\n           if perm is card:\n               continue\n           hook = getattr(perm, \"static_cost_reduction\", None)\n           if callable(hook):\n               raw += hook(game, card, controller)\n       ```\n       (inserted between `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)` and `card.controller = prev_controller`).\n     - cast_spell: after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player)`.\n     - cast_spell_free: same SpellCastTriggeredEvent firing after push.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` (MODIFIED): after attacker declaration loop in declare_attackers_step:\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent\n     for attacker in list(combat.attackers.keys()):\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n             game,\n             AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker),\n         )\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` (MODIFIED): added before BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent:\n     ```python\n     @dataclass\n     class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent):\n         player: Any = None\n         phase: Any = None\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` (MODIFIED): added branch in run_turn after the DRAW step branch:\n     ```python\n     elif current in ((Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None), (Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None)):\n         from engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n         game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n             game,\n             BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(\n                 player=game.active_player, phase=game.phase\n             ),\n         )\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` (CREATED, COMPLETE): TogetherAsOne(Sorcery), `{6}`. Helpers `_converge_count(card)` (handles int or list colors_spent → distinct count) and `_is_any_target(obj)` (player/creature/planeswalker). `__init__` sets `self.colors_spent = 0`. `get_targets` returns 2 TargetRequirements (target player filter `hasattr(obj,\"life\")`; any target filter `_is_any_target`), both zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD. `on_resolve`: X=_converge_count; if X<=0 return; chosen_targets[0]=player draws X (draw_card loop), chosen_targets[1]=damage target (deal_damage(game,self,target,X)), controller.life += X and fire GainsLifeTriggeredEvent.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` (CREATED, 9 tests, all passing): properties, targets, resolution (x=0 no-op, 3 colors draws/damages/gains, colors_spent as list, damage to creature).\n   - SOS card specs read (oracle texts) — all stubs are empty `class X(CardImpl): pass`:\n     - sos_1 The Dawning Archaic `{10}` Legendary Creature—Avatar 7/7: \"Costs {1} less per instant/sorcery in your graveyard. Reach. Whenever attacks, may cast target instant/sorcery from graveyard free; if it would go to graveyard, exile instead.\" complexity complex.\n     - sos_4 Together as One `{6}` Sorcery (DONE).\n     - sos_13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares `{1}{W}{W} // {W}` Creature—Cat Cleric // Instant 3/3, color [W]: ETB target player creates 1/1 white&black Inkling token w/ flying; then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, becomes prepared. Prepared (custom). complex.\n     - sos_57 Mana Sculpt `{1}{U}{U}` Instant: \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\" medium.\n     - sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer `{1}{B}{B}` Legendary Planeswalker—Ral loyalty 3: +1 Surveil 2; −1 Any number of target players each discard a card; −2 Return target creature card MV≤3 from your graveyard to battlefield; −7 Flip five coins, target opponent skips next X turns (X=heads). expert.\n     - sos_120 Improvisation Capstone `{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery—Lesson: \"Exile from top of library until total MV≥4, may cast any number free. Paradigm (then exile this spell; after you first resolve a spell with this name, may cast a copy from exile free at beginning of each of your first main phases).\" complex.\n     - sos_201 Lorehold, the Historian `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon 5/5: Flying, haste. Each I/S card in your hand has miracle {2}. At beginning of each opponent's upkeep, may discard a card; if so draw a card. expert.\n     - sos_226 Silverquill, the Disputant `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon 4/4 colors [B,W]: Flying, vigilance. Each I/S spell you cast has casualty 1. medium.\n     - sos_245 Witherbloom, the Balancer `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon 5/5 colors [B,G]: Affinity for creatures. Flying, deathtouch. I/S spells you cast have affinity for creatures. complex.\n     - sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex (Land): \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color, spend only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If not a creature, becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' Still a land.\" complex.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `python: command not found` — fixed by using `python3` (path /usr/bin/python3). No other errors; all tests passing.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed via grep that SpellCastTriggeredEvent and AttacksTriggeredEvent are defined but never fired anywhere in engine; engine_tests only register them (test_triggers.py) without firing via cast/combat, so adding firing is a safe no-op for existing tests. Verified: engine_tests 1145 passed, FDN tests 39 passed AFTER my engine edits.\n   - Resolved colors_spent ambiguity (real pipeline = list, grader/fdn_205 = int) with `_converge_count` handling both.\n   - Decided to add BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent + firing in turn.py to support Mana Sculpt's \"at the beginning of your next main phase\" delayed mana (engine had no main-phase event).\n   - Identified that skip-turns (Ral -7), miracle alternative cost (Lorehold), paradigm recursion (sos_120), prepared copy (sos_13), and casualty (Silverquill) are exotic mechanics requiring careful additive implementations; plan is faithful, deterministic, testable versions. Casualty plan: SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger on Silverquill that offers sacrifice of power≥1 creature then copies the spell via copy_spell.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (System-provided context at start: reads of PROJECT_MAP.md, test_utils.md, AGENTS.md, plus note test_utils.py/test_abilities.py too large; deferred-tools-via-ToolSearch reminder.)\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch loaded TaskCreate/TaskUpdate/TaskList).\n   - Multiple gentle system reminders: \"The task tools haven't been used recently... consider using TaskCreate/TaskUpdate... ignore if not applicable.\" (informational/optional).\n   - Final message (verbatim intent): \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks (task list IDs):\n   - #2 [in_progress] Implement sos_57 Mana Sculpt (counter + delayed mana).\n   - #3 Implement sos_226 Silverquill (casualty grant).\n   - #4 Implement sos_245 Witherbloom (affinity for creatures).\n   - #5 Implement sos_1 The Dawning Archaic.\n   - #6 Implement sos_13 Emeritus of Truce (Prepared).\n   - #7 Implement sos_97 Ral Zarek (Planeswalker).\n   - #8 Implement sos_120 Improvisation Capstone (Paradigm).\n   - #9 Implement sos_201 Lorehold (Miracle grant).\n   - #10 Implement sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex (Land).\n   - #11 Run pytest and fix failures.\n   - For each card: also write `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30 tests).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I was implementing **sos_57 Mana Sculpt** (task #2 in_progress). I had just completed the engine groundwork for it: added `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, phase)` to `engine/events.py` and added firing of it during precombat/postcombat main phases in `engine/turn.py` run_turn. I had NOT yet written `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` or its tests. The planned design for Mana Sculpt: Instant `{1}{U}{U}`; reuse the `_counter_spell`/`_get_chosen_target` pattern from fdn_48; `can_cast` returns True only when a spell is on the stack; `get_targets` returns a TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK) matching spells (excluding self); `on_resolve` counters the target spell, then if controller controls a Wizard (creature with subtype \"Wizard\" on battlefield), capture the countered spell's mana value (cmc) and register a one-shot delayed TriggerRegistration on `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (condition: event.player is controller) whose effect adds that many `ManaType.COLORLESS` to controller's pool then unregisters itself (source=self for identity-based unregister). I had NOT yet run anything after the turn.py edit.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` (ManaSculpt) implementing \"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add {C} equal to mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your next main phase\" using the counterspell pattern + the newly-added `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` delayed trigger, then write `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` and run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` to verify the new card works and no engine regressions occurred (since I just edited events.py and turn.py). This directly continues task #2 which was in progress. Verbatim from my work just before the interruption: I added to turn.py the `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` firing branch and stated the intent \"Started Mana Sculpt (sos_57): Added BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent to events.py (additive). Added firing in turn.py\" — next is writing the ManaSculpt card_impl.py itself.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/1995741a-49a1-4a45-a041-801f56ba31a7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1995741a-49a1-4a45-a041-801f56ba31a7","uuid":"152c65be-bb58-44e9-9273-71ad3089f63d","timestamp":"2026-06-02T06:57:10.870Z","isSynthetic":true}
