{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (set \"sos\") Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: card numbers **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a stub `card_impl.py` (empty class) to fill in. Plus write own tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30 tests per card).\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples.\n   - Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` via grep (961KB, don't read whole).\n   - For engine API discovery, read source modules directly (engine/card.py, events.py, triggers.py, replacement_effects.py, zones.py).\n   - \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics... you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n   - **CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim):** \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - AGENTS.md hard rules: card class must stay in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py` (no move/rename); `engine_tests/` read-only; do NOT edit FDN test files; **additive-only engine modifications** (may add methods/classes/files in `engine/` and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete anything existing in `engine/`).\n   - Final user message: respond with TEXT ONLY (no tool calls) and produce this summary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Python MTG engine. Class hierarchy: GameObject → CardImpl → {Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker, Land}. Creatures always include CardType.CREATURE; Instant/Sorcery auto-add their type.\n   - CardImpl hooks: `can_cast(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)->int` (generic-only, clamped ≥0), `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)` (reads `self.chosen_targets`), `get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers(game)`, `register_replacement_effects(game)`, `get_activated_abilities()`, `get_modes()`. Planeswalker adds `get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility]` (default []); Land adds `get_mana_abilities()`.\n   - Creature: `base_power/base_toughness` (printed), `modified_power/modified_toughness` (effects write here), `power`/`toughness` properties = modified + plus_one − minus_one. Constructor signature: `Creature(name, mana_cost, card_types, subtypes, supertypes, keywords, rules_text, owner, controller, base_power=0, base_toughness=0)`. `summoning_sick=True` by default. `_reset_characteristics()` resets modified P/T, counters, combat-restriction flags.\n   - Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=0, **kwargs): sets `self.loyalty = starting_loyalty`. LoyaltyAbility dataclass: `loyalty_cost: int`, `effect: Callable`, `description: str = \"\"`. Loyalty ability effects are `(game)->None` and read targets via `getattr(pw, '_resolve_target', None)` (see fdn_44 Kaito).\n   - Triggers: `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`. `game.trigger_manager.register/unregister(source identity-based)/fire_event(game, event)/get_triggers_for_source(source)`. fire_event matches by isinstance (subclasses included), APNAP order (active player's triggers first), pushes StackObject(source, controller, on_resolve=trigger.effect) — **the effect receives only `(game)`, NOT the event**. Returns early if no matching triggers. condition is `(game, event)->bool`.\n   - StackObject(source, controller, targets=[], on_resolve=lambda _game:None, is_mana_ability=False). `game.stack`: push/pop/peek/objects() (top→bottom)/is_empty()/_items (bottom→top list). copy_spell(game, original_stackobject, controller, new_targets=None) → shallow-copies source card, binds on_resolve to copied.on_resolve.\n   - priority_loop(game): resolves stack LIFO; DeterministicPlayer auto-passes when stack empty, else calls choose (needs scripted \"pass\").\n   - move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None): replacement effects consulted ONLY when `replacement_event is not None AND leaving_battlefield`. Fires LBF/dies/ETB events; for ENTERING battlefield fires ETB event BEFORE calling card.register_triggers (so a card's own self-ETB trigger registered in register_triggers will NOT catch its own entry during real play — FDN convention is to register-then-fire ETB manually in tests, see fdn_98).\n   - _resolve_spell: sets card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets, calls on_resolve; permanents→battlefield; instant/sorcery→graveyard (now exile if `replace_graveyard_with_exile`).\n   - casting: cast_spell (pays mana, sets card.colors_spent=list(last_payment_colors), fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent after push), cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone) (no mana/timing, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent). get_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)→max(0, min(raw, generic)) where raw = card.cost_reduction(game) + sum of battlefield perms' static_cost_reduction(game, card, controller). _apply_cost_reduction(cost, reduction).\n   - SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=StackObject, player, card, controller). event.spell is the StackObject (has .controller, .source, no card_types); event.card is the actual card (has card_types).\n   - Events (engine/events.py): TriggeredEvent base; EntersBattlefield, LeavesBattlefield, DealsDamage(source,target,amount,is_combat,combat), GainsLife(player,amount), DrawsCard, BeginningOfUpkeep, BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player,phase) [MY ADDITION], BeginningOfCombat, EndOfTurn, EndStep, CreatureDies, SpellCast, Attacks(creature,attacker), Blocks, CounterAdded. Replacement events: MoveToGraveyard(.card,.destination,.prevented), CreatureDies/PermanentDestroyed/Sacrifice subtypes, CreateToken, AddCounter.\n   - game.py helpers: deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice(game,player,permanent), exile(game,obj) (works from battlefield/gy/stack/hand → owner's exile), draw_card(game,player), discard, create_token(game,player,token) (sets is_token, fires ETB, registers triggers), add_counter(game,perm,counter_type,amount) (supports \"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\"), remove_counter, tap, untap. No gain_life helper — add `player.life += n` then fire GainsLifeTriggeredEvent.\n   - ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{U}{U}\"), .cmc (generic + sum(pips) + len(hybrid), X treated as 0), .generic, .pips, .x_count, .hybrid. ManaPool.add(ManaType,n)/get(ManaType)/total()/empty()/can_pay/pay/last_payment_colors. ManaType.COLORLESS. Color enum (WHITE..GREEN). Keyword Flag enum: FLYING, DEATHTOUCH(103), VIGILANCE(106), REACH(107), MENACE, FLASH, etc. `Keyword.X in card.keywords` works for Flag. Supertype.LEGENDARY(93).\n   - Zones: ZoneContainer (index 0=bottom, -1=top), add(obj, position=\"top\"/\"bottom\"), remove, contains (identity), get_all (bottom→top), top(n), shuffle. Per-player Zones for every Zone enum (incl EXILE). move_zone deletes colors_spent on zone change.\n   - test_utils: create_game(deck1, deck2, *, player1_name, player2_name, player1_life, player2_life, scripts=(s1,s2)); set_board_state(game, idx, *, battlefield, hand, graveyard, life, mana) (sets owner/controller; mana is dict[ManaType,int]); cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets) (requires empty stack for sorcery-speed); card_colors(card)->set[str] derived ONLY from mana cost pips (no card.colors attribute exists in engine).\n   - DeterministicPlayer: choose_target/choose/choose_yes_no/assign_damage_order/choose_card all pop (popleft) from `_script` deque; ScriptExhaustedError when empty. Scripts prepend in cast_spell via `_script.appendleft`.\n   - Environment: use `python3`. pytest.ini: `python_files = test