{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (set \"sos\") Magic: The Gathering card implementations in `/workspace/cards/sos/`: card numbers **1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257**. Each card directory has `card_spec.json` (metadata) and a stub `card_impl.py` (empty class) to fill in. Also write own tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py` (max 30 tests per card).\n   - Use completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples.\n   - Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` via grep (961KB, don't read whole).\n   - For engine API discovery, read source modules directly.\n   - \"You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics... you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n   - **CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim):** \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - AGENTS.md hard rules: card class must stay in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py` (no move/rename); `engine_tests/` read-only; do NOT edit FDN test files; **additive-only engine modifications** (may add methods/classes/files in `engine/` and modify bodies of existing functions, but MUST NOT rename/move/delete anything existing in `engine/`).\n   - Final user message: respond with TEXT ONLY (no tool calls) and produce this summary.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Python MTG engine. Class hierarchy: GameObject → CardImpl → {Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker, Land}.\n   - CardImpl hooks: can_cast(game) (default True), cost_reduction(game)->int (generic-only, clamped ≥0), on_cast(game), on_resolve(game) (reads self.chosen_targets), get_targets(game)->list[TargetRequirement], register_triggers(game), register_replacement_effects(game), get_activated_abilities()->list[ActivatedAbility], get_modes(), static_cost_reduction (custom additive hook from prior session).\n   - Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=0, **kwargs): sets self.loyalty; get_loyalty_abilities()->list[LoyaltyAbility] (default []). LoyaltyAbility dataclass: loyalty_cost:int, effect:Callable[(game)->None], description:str=\"\". Loyalty effects read targets via getattr(pw,'_resolve_target',None) singular or getattr(pw,'_resolve_targets',None) plural or getattr(pw,'_damage_assignments',None); set by tests directly. activate_ability/_activate_loyalty_ability pays loyalty, marks once-per-turn, pushes StackObject(on_resolve=ability.effect) — effect gets only (game).\n   - Land(**kwargs): adds CardType.LAND; can_cast returns False; get_mana_abilities()->list[ManaAbility] (default []). ManaAbility dataclass: cost:Callable[(game,src)->bool], mana_produced:Callable[(game)->None], description.\n   - ActivatedAbility dataclass: cost:Callable[(game,src)->bool] (checks+pays, returns bool), effect:Callable[(game)->None], description.\n   - Triggers: TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition:(game,event)->bool, effect:(game)->None, source, controller). game.trigger_manager.register/unregister(identity)/fire_event(game,event)/get_triggers_for_source(source). fire_event matches by isinstance + condition, pushes StackObject; effect receives ONLY (game) NOT event — capture event data via card-local \"pending\" list appended in condition (Silverquill/Lorehold pattern). Returns early (no push) if no matching trigger.\n   - StackObject(source, controller, targets=[], on_resolve, is_mana_ability=False). game.stack: push/pop/peek/is_empty.\n   - move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None) in engine/zones.py: handles ETB/LBF/dies events + register/unregister triggers; replacements only consulted when replacement_event not None AND leaving battlefield.\n   - casting.py: cast_spell (pays mana), cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone) (no mana/timing, finds card in any player's from_zone, fires SpellCastTriggeredEvent). _resolve_spell: permanents→battlefield, instant/sorcery→graveyard OR exile if `getattr(card,\"replace_graveyard_with_exile\",False)`. get_cost_reduction consults static_cost_reduction hooks.\n   - draw_card(game, player): increments player.cards_drawn_this_turn (was never reset before my change), fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card). discard(game, player, card). create_token(game, player, token). exile(game, obj). add_counter (supports \"+1/+1\",\"-1/-1\",\"loyalty\"). No gain_life helper (do player.life += n + fire GainsLifeTriggeredEvent).\n   - Events (events.py, dataclasses): EntersBattlefield, DealsDamage(source,target,amount,is_combat,combat), GainsLife(player,amount), DrawsCard(player,card), BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (NO fields — whose upkeep determined via game.active_player), BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player,phase) [my prior addition], EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent (no fields), EndStepTriggeredEvent(player), CreatureDies, SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell,player,card,controller) (event.spell=StackObject, event.card=actual card with card_types, event.controller=casting player), Attacks(creature,attacker).\n   - GameState.advance_phase: wrap-around uses extra_turns (FIFO) then _normal_next_index (flips). My skip logic added.\n   - turn.py run_turn: per-step actions; (ENDING,END) and (ENDING,CLEANUP); _NO_PRIORITY_STEPS={UNTAP, CLEANUP}.\n   - ManaCost.parse(\"{1}{B}{B}\"), .cmc, ManaCost(generic=N). ManaPool.add(ManaType,n)/total()/can_pay(cost)/pay(cost)/empty(). ManaType.{WHITE,BLUE,BLACK,RED,GREEN,COLORLESS}. Keyword Flag enum: FLYING, HASTE, DEATHTOUCH, VIGILANCE, REACH, FLASH. Supertype.LEGENDARY.\n   - Zones: ZoneContainer add(obj, position=\"top\"/\"bottom\"), remove, contains (identity), get_all (bottom→top), top(n) (top is last element). Per-player Zones incl LIBRARY, EXILE. move_to_zone deletes colors_spent on zone change.\n   - test_utils: create_game(deck1, deck2, *, player1_name, player2_name, player1_life, player2_life, scripts=(s1,s2)); set_board_state(game, idx, *, battlefield, hand, graveyard, life, mana) — NO library kwarg (populate library directly via player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY].add); card_colors(card)->set[str] derived from mana cost pips.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: choose_target/choose/choose_yes_no/assign_damage_order/choose_card pop from _script deque; ScriptExhaustedError when empty; _script.appendleft used by cast_spell helper.\n   - Environment: use `python3`. pytest.ini: python_files = test_*.py tests.py. \"Unknown config option: timeout\" warning is benign.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` (MODIFIED this session, additive):\n     - __init__ added after _normal_next_index: `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}`.\n     - advance_phase wrap-around rewritten to compute `candidate` (from extra_turns or _normal_next_index) then honor skips:\n       ```python\n       if self.skipped_turns:\n           guard = 0\n           while self.skipped_turns.get(candidate, 0) > 0 and guard < len(self.players):\n               self.skipped_turns[candidate] -= 1\n               if self.skipped_turns[candidate] <= 0:\n                   del self.skipped_turns[candidate]\n               candidate = 1 - candidate\n               self._normal_next_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index\n               guard += 1\n       self.active_player_index = candidate\n       ```\n       Only activates when skipped_turns is non-empty (no regression; default {}). Verified trace: skip flips both candidate and _normal_next_index so the skipped player resumes after.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py` (MODIFIED this session, additive): new helper after untap():\n     ```python\n     def flip_coin(game: GameState, player: Player | None = None) -> bool:\n         scripted = getattr(game, \"_scripted_coin_flips\", None)\n         if scripted:\n             return bool(scripted.pop(0))\n         import random\n         return random.choice([True, False])\n     ```\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` (MODIFIED this session, additive):\n     - _do_untap_step: after `active.land_plays_remaining = 1`, added:\n       ```python\n       for player in game.players:\n           player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0\n       ```\n     - run_turn: added elif before CLEANUP:\n       ```python\n       elif current == (Phase.ENDING, Step.END):\n           from engine.events import (EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent, EndStepTriggeredEvent)\n           game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, EndStepTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player))\n           game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent())\n       ```\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` (CREATED, COMPLETE): module helpers `_is_creature`, `_mana_value`, `_target_players(pw)` (reads _resolve_targets then _resolve_target), `surveil(game, player, amount)` (look at top `amount` via list(get_all())[-amount:], process reversed (top first), choose_yes_no put in graveyard). RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker): {1}{B}{B}, starting_loyalty=3, LEGENDARY, subtype \"Ral\". get_loyalty_abilities returns [+1 surveil 2, -1 each target player discards (reads _target_players, choose_card from hand, discard), -2 return target creature MV≤3 from your graveyard to battlefield (validate in gy + _is_creature + cmc≤3, move_to_zone GY→BATTLEFIELD), -7 flip 5 coins (engine.game.flip_coin) target opponent skips heads turns (game.skipped_turns[idx]+=heads; ignores self target / non-player)].\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` (CREATED, 23 tests pass): properties, surveil (incl helper empty library, keep all), discard (single/multiple/empty hand), reanimate (returns/rejects high MV/rejects noncreature/requires in graveyard), ultimate (skips per heads via game._scripted_coin_flips, zero heads no skip, ignores self), and TestSkipTurnMechanism with `_advance_one_turn` helper verifying skip-one/skip-two/normal rotation via repeated advance_phase.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` (CREATED, COMPLETE): helpers `_mana_value`, `_is_castable_spell` (not LAND), `exile_until_mana_value(game, controller, threshold)` (exile top until total MV≥threshold), `cast_free_from_exile(game, controller, cards)` (choose_yes_no per card, cast_spell_free from EXILE). ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery): {5}{R}{R}, subtype \"Lesson\", self.is_paradigm_copy=False. on_resolve: exile_until_mana_value(4) + cast_free_from_exile; if not is_paradigm_copy: set self.replace_graveyard_with_exile=True and _register_paradigm. _register_paradigm registers BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent trigger (condition: event.player is controller AND event.phase==Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN; effect: if original still in exile, choose_yes_no, create copy with is_paradigm_copy=True, add to exile, cast_spell_free).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py` (CREATED, 17 tests pass): properties, exile_until (stops at threshold/single big/empty/exhausts), main effect (casts chosen for free via _Pinger game._resolved, decline leaves in exile), paradigm (arms on resolve: replace flag True + 1 trigger; copy does not arm; recurs on first main; skips postcombat main; only controller triggers).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` (CREATED, COMPLETE): MIRACLE_COST=ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"), `_is_instant_or_sorcery`, `cast_for_miracle(game, controller, card, miracle_cost)` (require card in hand, can_pay miracle_cost, pay, cast_spell_free from HAND; returns bool). LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature): {3}{R}{W}, LEGENDARY, subtypes {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, FLYING|HASTE, 5/5, self._miracle_pending=[]. register_triggers registers 2: (a) DrawsCardTriggeredEvent miracle — condition: event.player is controller AND controller controls source AND _is_instant_or_sorcery(card) AND controller.cards_drawn_this_turn==1, appends card to _miracle_pending; effect pops, choose_yes_no, cast_for_miracle. (b) BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent loot — condition: controller controls source AND game.active_player is not controller; effect: choose_yes_no, choose_card, discard, draw_card.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` (CREATED, 18 tests pass): properties (incl registers_two_triggers), miracle (first drawn instant castable, decline keeps, can't pay, noninstant skip, not-first-draw skip, cast_for_miracle helper), loot (loots on opponent upkeep, no loot own upkeep, decline, empty hand no crash). Uses _Bolt(Instant) game._resolved.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` (CREATED this session, COMPLETE — last action): GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land). __init__ sets inert creature attrs (base_power/toughness=0, modified_power/toughness=0, plus_one/minus_one_counters=0, damage_marked=0, _pump=0). Properties power (modified_power+plus_one-minus_one+_pump), toughness, is_creature. get_mana_abilities returns 2: {T}:Add {C}; {T},Pay 1 life:Add any color (choose color; restriction not enforced — engine limitation note). get_activated_abilities returns 1 ActivatedAbility ({5}: cost checks not-creature + total≥5 + pay ManaCost(generic=5); effect calls animate). animate(game): if not already CREATURE, add CREATURE type + \"Wizard\" subtype, set base/modified P/T 2/4, set is_attacking/is_blocking=False, summoning_sick=False, then _register_creature_triggers. _register_creature_triggers registers SpellCastTriggeredEvent (+1 _pump when controller casts instant/sorcery) and EndStepTriggeredEvent (reset _pump=0).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_spec.json` (READ): Land. Oracle: \"{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.\\n{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \\\"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\\\" It's still a land.\" colors [] (colorless).\n   - Referenced (read-only): fdn_44 (Kaito loyalty), fdn_81 (Chandra _resolve_targets), fdn_28 (Vanguard Seraph surveil), fdn_267 (Secluded Courtyard mana abilities), fdn_106 (ActivatedAbility cost pays ManaCost(generic=6), src.is_tapped).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No test failures this session; every card's tests passed on first run (sos_97: 23, sos_120: 17, sos_201: 18).\n   - Discovered cards_drawn_this_turn is never reset by the engine → \"first card drawn this turn\" couldn't be computed → fixed by adding additive reset in _do_untap_step. Verified safe (engine_tests 1145 passed).\n   - Discovered EndStepTriggeredEvent/EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent are never fired by the engine (also affects fdn_81's \"until end of turn\") → added additive firing at (ENDING,END) in run_turn. Verified safe (engine_tests + FDN: 1184 passed).\n   - Avoided known pitfalls: trigger effects receive only (game) not event (used pending-list capture in conditions); self-ETB triggers won't self-fire during real move_to_zone (tests register_triggers then fire manually, FDN convention).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Ral's skip-turn: additive game.skipped_turns dict honored in advance_phase, preserving 2-player alternation by flipping _normal_next_index per skip; deterministic coin flips via game._scripted_coin_flips seam in flip_coin.\n   - Improvisation Capstone Paradigm: self-exile via replace_graveyard_with_exile + recurring BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent trigger; copies flagged is_paradigm_copy to prevent infinite re-arming.\n   - Lorehold miracle: draw-triggered grant with pending-list; pays {2} then cast_spell_free; required cards_drawn_this_turn reset.\n   - Great Hall manland (no engine precedent): animate by mutating the Land instance (add CREATURE type, set P/T, register cast + end-step triggers); power/toughness as class properties using _pump for the +1/+0 until-end-of-turn.\n\n6. All user messages (this session):\n   - (Session-start: 6 system-reminder Read results for sos_13 tests/impl, sos_1 tests/impl; note casting.py too large; deferred-tools-via-ToolSearch list; then the continuation prompt to resume task #7.)\n   - \"Tool loaded.\" (after ToolSearch loaded TaskUpdate).\n   - Multiple gentle reminders: \"The task tools haven't been used recently... consider using TaskCreate/TaskUpdate... ignore if not applicable.\" (optional/informational).\n   - Final message (verbatim core): \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n   - Preserved security/process constraints (still in effect): do NOT modify anything under `workspace/engine_tests/`; additive-only engine edits (no rename/move/delete of existing engine items); keep card class in its card_impl.py; don't edit FDN tests; max 30 tests per card; use python3.\n\n7. Pending Tasks (task IDs):\n   - #10 [in_progress] Implement sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex — card_impl.py DONE; still need to write `cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` (max 30 tests) and run them.\n   - #11 [pending] Run pytest and fix failures (full suite final check).\n   - Completed this session: #7 sos_97, #8 sos_120, #9 sos_201. Completed prior: #1-#6.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary I had just written `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` (GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex Land, COMPLETE) as the final action — the Write tool returned \"File created successfully.\" I had NOT yet written tests for sos_257, and had NOT run sos_257 tests. Prior to writing the card I made the additive turn.py change to fire EndStepTriggeredEvent + EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent at (ENDING, END) and verified engine_tests + cards/fdn pass (1184 passed). The card uses: two ManaAbility ({T}:Add {C}; {T},Pay 1 life:any color), one ActivatedAbility ({5}: animate), and an animate(game) method that adds CardType.CREATURE + \"Wizard\", sets 2/4 P/T, and registers a SpellCastTriggeredEvent +1/+0 trigger plus an EndStepTriggeredEvent _pump-reset trigger.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py` (≤30 tests) covering: Land properties (is Land, name, no mana cost, colorless, LAND type, starts non-creature); {T}:Add {C} mana ability (taps, adds COLORLESS); {T},Pay 1 life mana ability (taps, life-1, adds chosen color, fails when already tapped/life 0); {5} activate cost (fails if <5 mana or already creature, pays 5); animate (adds CREATURE+Wizard, power==2/toughness==4, still LAND, registers 2 triggers, idempotent); cast-trigger +1/+0 (power 3 after casting an instant/sorcery via SpellCastTriggeredEvent, only for controller); end-step reset (_pump→0 after EndStepTriggeredEvent). Then run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` to verify the card and no engine regressions. After that, complete task #11: run the full suite `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/ engine_tests/ cards/fdn/ -q` and fix any failures. This directly continues task #10 (in_progress), whose card_impl.py was just completed and which still requires its tests.tests.py per the standing requirement \"Plus write own tests at cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py (max 30 tests per card).\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/1995741a-49a1-4a45-a041-801f56ba31a7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1995741a-49a1-4a45-a041-801f56ba31a7","uuid":"ea7b7c1e-1aff-4e6d-8382-b4bdddd5b2ad","timestamp":"2026-06-02T07:31:26.144Z","isSynthet